  "facts": [
    "Pakokku Bridge, Myanmar's longest, stretches 3.4 km across the Irrawaddy, linking Pakokku town with Nyaung‑U district and forming a vital spine of the India–Myanmar–Thailand Trilateral Highway.",
    "Inaugurated on 1 January 2012 by Vice‑President Tin Aung Myint Oo, the bridge boasts a 28‑foot wide motorway, a 14‑foot roadway, and dual pedestrian walkways, all set atop a 52‑foot high, 262‑foot wide clearance span.",
    "Engineering marvels include a 512‑foot approach bridge and an 850‑foot embankment, while the broad‑crested design ensures robust support for both rail and road traffic across Myanmar's largest river crossing."
